{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01R7yPVJtntJao559hPgZA3p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the task carefully. I need to:\n\n1. Create `cmd/version/main.go` - a standalone binary that prints version\n2. Create `.golangci.yml` - golangci-lint configuration\n3. Verify that existing magefiles satisfy requirements R2 and R4\n\nLet me first read the required documents that are NOT in the project_context (or that need to be read from the filesystem). The task says I can only use tools to read files NOT already provided in project_context.\n\nLooking at the files listed in required_reading:\n- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml` - provided in project_context\n- `docs/specs/product-requirements/prd011-magefiles.yaml` - listed in repository_files but NOT in project_context\n\n\n- `docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc001-magefiles.yaml` - also listed in repository_files but NOT in project_context\n- `magefiles/magefile.go` - the required_reading mentions this, but the repository file listing shows `magefiles/orchestrator.go` instead, so I need to verify which file actually exists\n\nNow I'm checking what else is in repository_files but missing from project_context: `go.mod`, `magefiles/go.mod`, `magefiles/go.sum`, and a couple of spec files. I should read these to understand the existing setup, though I need to be careful about the constraint against reading files just to infer patterns. use tools to read files that are NOT already provided above.\"\n\nSo I CAN read files that are in repository_files but NOT in project_context. Let me read the necessary ones.\n\nThe required_reading mentions `magefiles/magefile.go` but the repository file list has `magefiles/orchestrator.go`. Let me read the relevant files.\n\nFiles I need to read (from repository_files, not in project_context):\n1. `docs/specs/product-requirements/prd011-magefiles.yaml` - Required Reading\n2. `docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc001-magefiles.yaml` - Required Reading\n3. `magefiles/orchestrator.go` - Referenced as magefiles/magefile.go in required_reading (likely the same concept)\n4. `go.mod` - Need to know module name and Go version\n5. `magefiles/go.mod` - Need to understand the magefiles module setup\n\nLet me start reading these files to understand the project structure and requirements.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23911,"cache_read_input_tokens":15967,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23911},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1e27269-084c-48a0-81f5-e7539000574e","uuid":"c8b8de4a-5595-4ada-80dc-d3220722e986"}
