{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jvtn34BgpepLyfGajM5jku","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel00.0-uc001-magefiles\n     2→title: \"Build, lint, and version-check via mage targets\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator runs mage build to compile cmd/version to bin/version, verifies that the\n     6→  binary prints the repository's version tag, runs mage lint to confirm no warnings, and\n     7→  runs mage clean to remove build artifacts. This exercises the full build lifecycle\n     8→  specified in prd011-magefiles before any utility code exists.\n     9→\n    10→actor: Human Operator\n    11→\n    12→trigger: |\n    13→  The operator has completed the PRD (prd011-magefiles.yaml) and wants to verify that the\n    14→  build pipeline produces a working binary.\n    15→\n    16→flow:\n    17→  - id: F1\n    18→    step: |\n    19→      The operator runs mage build. The target compiles every package under cmd/ to bin/.\n    20→      For cmd/version, the target resolves the latest version tag via\n    21→      git describe --tags --abbrev=0 --match \"v[0-9]*\" and passes it through -ldflags.\n    22→  - id: F2\n    23→    step: |\n    24→      The operator runs bin/version. The binary prints the version tag (e.g., \"v0.20260228.0\")\n    25→      to stdout followed by a newline and exits 0.\n    26→  - id: F3\n    27→    step: |\n    28→      The operator runs bin/version --version. The output is identical to F2.\n    29→  - id: F4\n    30→    step: |\n    31→      The operator runs bin/version --bogus. The binary prints a usage message to stderr\n    32→      and exits 2.\n    33→  - id: F5\n    34→    step: |\n    35→      The operator runs mage lint. golangci-lint runs on cmd/, pkg/, and magefiles/ with\n    36→      no warnings or errors.\n    37→  - id: F6\n    38→    step: |\n    39→      The operator runs mage clean. The bin/ directory and its contents are removed. If\n    40→      bin/ does not exist, the target succeeds silently.\n    41→  - id: F7\n    42→    step: |\n    43→      The operator verifies that bin/ no longer exists after mage clean.\n    44→\n    45→touchpoints:\n    46→  - T1: \"cmd/version — version string printing, ldflags injection (prd011-magefiles R1)\"\n    47→  - T2: \"magefiles/ — build, lint, clean targets (prd011-magefiles R2, R3, R4)\"\n    48→  - T3: \"configuration.yaml — project.binary_dir, project.go_source_dirs (prd011-magefiles R6)\"\n    49→\n    50→success_criteria:\n    51→  - id: S1\n    52→    criterion: mage build succeeds and bin/version exists.\n    53→  - id: S2\n    54→    criterion: bin/version prints a version tag matching v[0-9]* and exits 0.\n    55→  - id: S3\n    56→    criterion: bin/version --version produces the same output as bin/version.\n    57→  - id: S4\n    58→    criterion: bin/version --bogus prints to stderr and exits 2.\n    59→  - id: S5\n    60→    criterion: mage lint passes with no warnings on cmd/, pkg/, and magefiles/.\n    61→  - id: S6\n    62→    criterion: mage clean removes bin/ and succeeds when bin/ does not exist.\n    63→  - id: S7\n    64→    criterion: A development build (no ldflags) produces a binary that prints \"dev\".\n    65→\n    66→out_of_scope:\n    67→  - Differential testing of cmd/version against a reference binary (there is no GNU version equivalent).\n    68→  - mage install is exercised by the operator manually; it is not part of this use case's primary flow.\n    69→  - Orchestrator, generator, scaffold, and prompt targets are provided by cobbler-scaffold and not covered here.\n    70→\n    71→test_suite: test-rel00.0\n    72→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1e27269-084c-48a0-81f5-e7539000574e","uuid":"83ae94ea-0b64-4bdf-ad5b-5b9feb7442c0","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/290/docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc001-magefiles.yaml","content":"id: rel00.0-uc001-magefiles\ntitle: \"Build, lint, and version-check via mage targets\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator runs mage build to compile cmd/version to bin/version, verifies that the\n  binary prints the repository's version tag, runs mage lint to confirm no warnings, and\n  runs mage clean to remove build artifacts. This exercises the full build lifecycle\n  specified in prd011-magefiles before any utility code exists.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD (prd011-magefiles.yaml) and wants to verify that the\n  build pipeline produces a working binary.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs mage build. The target compiles every package under cmd/ to bin/.\n      For cmd/version, the target resolves the latest version tag via\n      git describe --tags --abbrev=0 --match \"v[0-9]*\" and passes it through -ldflags.\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      The operator runs bin/version. The binary prints the version tag (e.g., \"v0.20260228.0\")\n      to stdout followed by a newline and exits 0.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      The operator runs bin/version --version. The output is identical to F2.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The operator runs bin/version --bogus. The binary prints a usage message to stderr\n      and exits 2.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The operator runs mage lint. golangci-lint runs on cmd/, pkg/, and magefiles/ with\n      no warnings or errors.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      The operator runs mage clean. The bin/ directory and its contents are removed. If\n      bin/ does not exist, the target succeeds silently.\n  - id: F7\n    step: |\n      The operator verifies that bin/ no longer exists after mage clean.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/version — version string printing, ldflags injection (prd011-magefiles R1)\"\n  - T2: \"magefiles/ — build, lint, clean targets (prd011-magefiles R2, R3, R4)\"\n  - T3: \"configuration.yaml — project.binary_dir, project.go_source_dirs (prd011-magefiles R6)\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: mage build succeeds and bin/version exists.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: bin/version prints a version tag matching v[0-9]* and exits 0.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: bin/version --version produces the same output as bin/version.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: bin/version --bogus prints to stderr and exits 2.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: mage lint passes with no warnings on cmd/, pkg/, and magefiles/.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: mage clean removes bin/ and succeeds when bin/ does not exist.\n  - id: S7\n    criterion: A development build (no ldflags) produces a binary that prints \"dev\".\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - Differential testing of cmd/version against a reference binary (there is no GNU version equivalent).\n  - mage install is exercised by the operator manually; it is not part of this use case's primary flow.\n  - Orchestrator, generator, scaffold, and prompt targets are provided by cobbler-scaffold and not covered here.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel00.0\n","numLines":72,"startLine":1,"totalLines":72}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012ninZTJCsgs5WkWm8xLXZj","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: prd011-magefiles\n     2→title: \"magefiles and cmd/version: Build Lifecycle and Version Identity\"\n     3→\n     4→problem: |\n     5→  go-unix-utils has no testable artifact until its first utility passes differential tests.\n     6→  The mage build targets (build, lint, clean, install) are inherited from cobbler-scaffold's\n     7→  orchestrator library, but the project has no specification for what those targets must do\n     8→  in this repository. Without a PRD the build lifecycle is an undocumented dependency of\n     9→  every other PRD.\n    10→\n    11→  A second gap is version identity. The project tags documentation releases (v0.YYYYMMDD.N)\n    12→  and code releases (v1.YYYYMMDD.N), but no binary reports which version it was built from.\n    13→  A cmd/version binary that prints the last known version tag gives a concrete, testable\n    14→  artifact that exercises the full build pipeline (compile, lint, test, install) before any\n    15→  utility code exists. It also provides a version string that other cmd/ binaries can import\n    16→  when they need to report their own version.\n    17→\n    18→goals:\n    19→  - G1: Specify a cmd/version binary that prints the repository's last known version tag.\n    20→  - G2: Specify the build target that compiles all cmd/ binaries to bin/.\n    21→  - G3: Specify the lint target that runs golangci-lint on all Go source.\n    22→  - G4: Specify the clean target that removes build artifacts.\n    23→  - G5: Specify the install target that runs go install for cmd/ binaries.\n    24→  - G6: Specify the configuration contract between magefiles/ and configuration.yaml for the fields consumed by these targets.\n    25→\n    26→requirements:\n    27→  R1:\n    28→    title: cmd/version binary\n    29→    items:\n    30→      - R1.1: |\n    31→          Must provide a cmd/version/ package that compiles to a standalone binary. When\n    32→          invoked with no arguments, the binary prints the version string to stdout followed\n    33→          by a newline and exits 0.\n    34→      - R1.2: |\n    35→          The version string must be set at build time via -ldflags \"-X main.version=<tag>\".\n    36→          When the linker variable is not set (development builds), the binary must print\n    37→          \"dev\" as the version string.\n    38→      - R1.3: |\n    39→          The mage build target must resolve the version tag by running\n    40→          git describe --tags --abbrev=0 --match \"v[0-9]*\" and passing the result to the\n    41→          linker. If the git command fails (no tags, not a git repository), the build must\n    42→          succeed with the version set to \"dev\".\n    43→      - R1.4: |\n    44→          When invoked with --version or -v, the binary must print the same version string\n    45→          as the no-argument invocation. Any other flag must cause the binary to print a\n    46→          usage message to stderr and exit 2.\n    47→      - R1.5: |\n    48→          The version package must export a variable or function so that other cmd/ packages\n    49→          can import and report the same version string without duplicating the ldflags\n    50→          mechanism.\n    51→\n    52→  R2:\n    53→    title: Build target\n    54→    items:\n    55→      - R2.1: |\n    56→          mage build must compile every package under cmd/ to a binary in the directory\n    57→          specified by configuration.yaml project.binary_dir (default: bin/). Each binary\n    58→          is named after its cmd/ subdirectory (e.g., cmd/version/ produces bin/version).\n    59→      - R2.2: |\n    60→          mage build must pass -ldflags with the version tag resolved per R1.3 to every\n    61→          cmd/ binary that imports the version variable.\n    62→      - R2.3: |\n    63→          mage build must fail with a non-zero exit code if any cmd/ package fails to\n    64→          compile. The error message must identify which package failed.\n    65→      - R2.4: |\n    66→          mage build must create the binary_dir if it does not exist.\n    67→\n    68→  R3:\n    69→    title: Lint target\n    70→    items:\n    71→      - R3.1: |\n    72→          mage lint must run golangci-lint on all Go source directories listed in\n    73→          configuration.yaml project.go_source_dirs (default: pkg, cmd). The linter\n    74→          must also cover magefiles/.\n    75→      - R3.2: |\n    76→          mage lint must fail with a non-zero exit code if golangci-lint reports any\n    77→          warnings or errors.\n    78→      - R3.3: |\n    79→          The golangci-lint configuration must be committed to the repository (as\n    80→          .golangci.yml or equivalent) so that lint results are reproducible.\n    81→\n    82→  R4:\n    83→    title: Clean target\n    84→    items:\n    85→      - R4.1: |\n    86→          mage clean must remove the binary_dir and all its contents. If the directory\n    87→          does not exist, the target must succeed silently.\n    88→      - R4.2: |\n    89→          mage clean must not remove source files, documentation, or any directory\n    90→          outside binary_dir.\n    91→\n    92→  R5:\n    93→    title: Install target\n    94→    items:\n    95→      - R5.1: |\n    96→          mage install must run go install for every package under cmd/, installing\n    97→          binaries to the Go bin directory ($GOPATH/bin or $GOBIN).\n    98→      - R5.2: |\n    99→          mage install must pass the same -ldflags as mage build (R2.2).\n   100→\n   101→  R6:\n   102→    title: Configuration contract\n   103→    items:\n   104→      - R6.1: |\n   105→          The following fields in configuration.yaml project section are consumed by the\n   106→          build lifecycle targets and must be present:\n   107→\n   108→            project.module_path    — Go module path (used by go build)\n   109→            project.binary_dir     — output directory for compiled binaries (default: bin)\n   110→            project.go_source_dirs — list of directories containing Go source (default: [pkg, cmd])\n   111→            project.magefiles_dir  — directory containing mage targets (default: magefiles)\n   112→      - R6.2: |\n   113→          magefiles/orchestrator.go must load configuration.yaml at init time via the\n   114→          orchestrator library. If the file does not exist, the init function must create\n   115→          a default configuration file and log the action to stderr.\n   116→      - R6.3: |\n   117→          Build lifecycle targets (build, lint, clean, install) must not depend on fields\n   118→          outside the project section of configuration.yaml. Orchestrator, cobbler, and\n   119→          claude sections are consumed by cobbler-scaffold targets, not by this PRD's scope.\n   120→\n   121→non_goals:\n   122→  - This PRD does not specify orchestrator targets (cobbler:measure, cobbler:stitch). Those are provided by cobbler-scaffold.\n   123→  - This PRD does not specify generator lifecycle targets (generator:start, generator:run, generator:stop). Those are provided by cobbler-scaffold.\n   124→  - This PRD does not specify scaffold, prompt, or stats targets. Those are provided by cobbler-scaffold.\n   125→  - This PRD does not specify the analyze target. Cross-artifact consistency checks are provided by cobbler-scaffold.\n   126→  - cmd/version does not parse LS_COLORS, handle signals, or do anything beyond printing a version string.\n   127→\n   128→acceptance_criteria:\n   129→  - \"AC1: mage build compiles cmd/version/ to bin/version. Running bin/version prints a version tag string (matching v[0-9]*) followed by a newline and exits 0.\"\n   130→  - \"AC2: bin/version --version prints the same output as bin/version with no arguments.\"\n   131→  - \"AC3: bin/version --bogus prints a usage message to stderr and exits 2.\"\n   132→  - \"AC4: A development build (without ldflags) produces a binary that prints \\\"dev\\\".\"\n   133→  - \"AC5: mage lint runs golangci-lint on cmd/, pkg/, and magefiles/ with no warnings.\"\n   134→  - \"AC6: mage clean removes bin/ and succeeds silently when bin/ does not exist.\"\n   135→  - \"AC7: mage build followed by mage clean followed by ls bin/ shows bin/ does not exist.\"\n   136→  - \"AC8: All configuration fields consumed by build lifecycle targets are documented in R6.1 and present in configuration.yaml.\"\n   137→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1e27269-084c-48a0-81f5-e7539000574e","uuid":"f3cab828-f9a1-441b-bf58-b7b1e19aff4d","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/290/docs/specs/product-requirements/prd011-magefiles.yaml","content":"id: prd011-magefiles\ntitle: \"magefiles and cmd/version: Build Lifecycle and Version Identity\"\n\nproblem: |\n  go-unix-utils has no testable artifact until its first utility passes differential tests.\n  The mage build targets (build, lint, clean, install) are inherited from cobbler-scaffold's\n  orchestrator library, but the project has no specification for what those targets must do\n  in this repository. Without a PRD the build lifecycle is an undocumented dependency of\n  every other PRD.\n\n  A second gap is version identity. The project tags documentation releases (v0.YYYYMMDD.N)\n  and code releases (v1.YYYYMMDD.N), but no binary reports which version it was built from.\n  A cmd/version binary that prints the last known version tag gives a concrete, testable\n  artifact that exercises the full build pipeline (compile, lint, test, install) before any\n  utility code exists. It also provides a version string that other cmd/ binaries can import\n  when they need to report their own version.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Specify a cmd/version binary that prints the repository's last known version tag.\n  - G2: Specify the build target that compiles all cmd/ binaries to bin/.\n  - G3: Specify the lint target that runs golangci-lint on all Go source.\n  - G4: Specify the clean target that removes build artifacts.\n  - G5: Specify the install target that runs go install for cmd/ binaries.\n  - G6: Specify the configuration contract between magefiles/ and configuration.yaml for the fields consumed by these targets.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: cmd/version binary\n    items:\n      - R1.1: |\n          Must provide a cmd/version/ package that compiles to a standalone binary. When\n          invoked with no arguments, the binary prints the version string to stdout followed\n          by a newline and exits 0.\n      - R1.2: |\n          The version string must be set at build time via -ldflags \"-X main.version=<tag>\".\n          When the linker variable is not set (development builds), the binary must print\n          \"dev\" as the version string.\n      - R1.3: |\n          The mage build target must resolve the version tag by running\n          git describe --tags --abbrev=0 --match \"v[0-9]*\" and passing the result to the\n          linker. If the git command fails (no tags, not a git repository), the build must\n          succeed with the version set to \"dev\".\n      - R1.4: |\n          When invoked with --version or -v, the binary must print the same version string\n          as the no-argument invocation. Any other flag must cause the binary to print a\n          usage message to stderr and exit 2.\n      - R1.5: |\n          The version package must export a variable or function so that other cmd/ packages\n          can import and report the same version string without duplicating the ldflags\n          mechanism.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Build target\n    items:\n      - R2.1: |\n          mage build must compile every package under cmd/ to a binary in the directory\n          specified by configuration.yaml project.binary_dir (default: bin/). Each binary\n          is named after its cmd/ subdirectory (e.g., cmd/version/ produces bin/version).\n      - R2.2: |\n          mage build must pass -ldflags with the version tag resolved per R1.3 to every\n          cmd/ binary that imports the version variable.\n      - R2.3: |\n          mage build must fail with a non-zero exit code if any cmd/ package fails to\n          compile. The error message must identify which package failed.\n      - R2.4: |\n          mage build must create the binary_dir if it does not exist.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Lint target\n    items:\n      - R3.1: |\n          mage lint must run golangci-lint on all Go source directories listed in\n          configuration.yaml project.go_source_dirs (default: pkg, cmd). The linter\n          must also cover magefiles/.\n      - R3.2: |\n          mage lint must fail with a non-zero exit code if golangci-lint reports any\n          warnings or errors.\n      - R3.3: |\n          The golangci-lint configuration must be committed to the repository (as\n          .golangci.yml or equivalent) so that lint results are reproducible.\n\n  R4:\n    title: Clean target\n    items:\n      - R4.1: |\n          mage clean must remove the binary_dir and all its contents. If the directory\n          does not exist, the target must succeed silently.\n      - R4.2: |\n          mage clean must not remove source files, documentation, or any directory\n          outside binary_dir.\n\n  R5:\n    title: Install target\n    items:\n      - R5.1: |\n          mage install must run go install for every package under cmd/, installing\n          binaries to the Go bin directory ($GOPATH/bin or $GOBIN).\n      - R5.2: |\n          mage install must pass the same -ldflags as mage build (R2.2).\n\n  R6:\n    title: Configuration contract\n    items:\n      - R6.1: |\n          The following fields in configuration.yaml project section are consumed by the\n          build lifecycle targets and must be present:\n\n            project.module_path    — Go module path (used by go build)\n            project.binary_dir     — output directory for compiled binaries (default: bin)\n            project.go_source_dirs — list of directories containing Go source (default: [pkg, cmd])\n            project.magefiles_dir  — directory containing mage targets (default: magefiles)\n      - R6.2: |\n          magefiles/orchestrator.go must load configuration.yaml at init time via the\n          orchestrator library. If the file does not exist, the init function must create\n          a default configuration file and log the action to stderr.\n      - R6.3: |\n          Build lifecycle targets (build, lint, clean, install) must not depend on fields\n          outside the project section of configuration.yaml. Orchestrator, cobbler, and\n          claude sections are consumed by cobbler-scaffold targets, not by this PRD's scope.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - This PRD does not specify orchestrator targets (cobbler:measure, cobbler:stitch). Those are provided by cobbler-scaffold.\n  - This PRD does not specify generator lifecycle targets (generator:start, generator:run, generator:stop). Those are provided by cobbler-scaffold.\n  - This PRD does not specify scaffold, prompt, or stats targets. Those are provided by cobbler-scaffold.\n  - This PRD does not specify the analyze target. Cross-artifact consistency checks are provided by cobbler-scaffold.\n  - cmd/version does not parse LS_COLORS, handle signals, or do anything beyond printing a version string.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - \"AC1: mage build compiles cmd/version/ to bin/version. Running bin/version prints a version tag string (matching v[0-9]*) followed by a newline and exits 0.\"\n  - \"AC2: bin/version --version prints the same output as bin/version with no arguments.\"\n  - \"AC3: bin/version --bogus prints a usage message to stderr and exits 2.\"\n  - \"AC4: A development build (without ldflags) produces a binary that prints \\\"dev\\\".\"\n  - \"AC5: mage lint runs golangci-lint on cmd/, pkg/, and magefiles/ with no warnings.\"\n  - \"AC6: mage clean removes bin/ and succeeds silently when bin/ does not exist.\"\n  - \"AC7: mage build followed by mage clean followed by ls bin/ shows bin/ does not exist.\"\n  - \"AC8: All configuration fields consumed by build lifecycle targets are documented in R6.1 and present in configuration.yaml.\"\n","numLines":137,"startLine":1,"totalLines":137}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G4KatuyjJR3prXyRErdkfi","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     2→// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     3→\n     4→package main\n     5→\n     6→import (\n     7→\t\"errors\"\n     8→\t\"fmt\"\n     9→\t\"os\"\n    10→\t\"time\"\n    11→\n    12→\t\"github.com/magefile/mage/mg\"\n    13→\t\"github.com/mesh-intelligence/cobbler-scaffold/pkg/orchestrator\"\n    14→)\n    15→\n    16→// Cobbler groups the measure and stitch targets.\n    17→type Cobbler mg.Namespace\n    18→\n    19→// Generator groups the code-generation trail lifecycle targets.\n    20→type Generator mg.Namespace\n    21→\n    22→// Scaffold groups the scaffold install/uninstall targets.\n    23→type Scaffold mg.Namespace\n    24→\n    25→// Prompt groups prompt preview targets.\n    26→type Prompt mg.Namespace\n    27→\n    28→// Stats groups the stats targets (LOC, tokens).\n    29→type Stats mg.Namespace\n    30→\n    31→// Tests: run directly with go test:\n    32→//   go test -tags=usecase -v -count=1 -timeout 1800s ./tests/rel01.0/...          # all\n    33→//   go test -tags=usecase -v ./tests/rel01.0/uc001/                               # one UC\n    34→//   go test -tags=usecase -bench=. -benchtime=1x -run=^$ ./tests/rel01.0/uc008/   # benchmarks\n    35→\n    36→// baseCfg holds the configuration loaded from configuration.yaml.\n    37→var baseCfg orchestrator.Config\n    38→\n    39→func init() {\n    40→\tif _, err := os.Stat(orchestrator.DefaultConfigFile); errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n    41→\t\tif err := orchestrator.WriteDefaultConfig(orchestrator.DefaultConfigFile); err != nil {\n    42→\t\t\tpanic(fmt.Sprintf(\"creating %s: %v\", orchestrator.DefaultConfigFile, err))\n    43→\t\t}\n    44→\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"created default %s\\n\", orchestrator.DefaultConfigFile)\n    45→\t}\n    46→\tvar err error\n    47→\tbaseCfg, err = orchestrator.LoadConfig(orchestrator.DefaultConfigFile)\n    48→\tif err != nil {\n    49→\t\tpanic(fmt.Sprintf(\"loading %s: %v\", orchestrator.DefaultConfigFile, err))\n    50→\t}\n    51→}\n    52→\n    53→// newOrch creates an Orchestrator from the base config.\n    54→func newOrch() *orchestrator.Orchestrator {\n    55→\treturn orchestrator.New(baseCfg)\n    56→}\n    57→\n    58→// logf prints a timestamped log line to stderr.\n    59→func logf(format string, args ...any) {\n    60→\tmsg := fmt.Sprintf(format, args...)\n    61→\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"[%s] %s\\n\", time.Now().Format(time.RFC3339), msg)\n    62→}\n    63→\n    64→// --- Top-level targets ---\n    65→\n    66→// Init initializes the project.\n    67→func Init() error { return newOrch().Init() }\n    68→\n    69→// Reset performs a full reset: cobbler and generator.\n    70→func Reset() error { return newOrch().FullReset() }\n    71→\n    72→// Build compiles the project binary.\n    73→func Build() error { return newOrch().Build() }\n    74→\n    75→// Lint runs golangci-lint on the project.\n    76→func Lint() error { return newOrch().Lint() }\n    77→\n    78→// Install runs go install for the main package.\n    79→func Install() error { return newOrch().Install() }\n    80→\n    81→// Clean removes build artifacts.\n    82→func Clean() error { return newOrch().Clean() }\n    83→\n    84→// Credentials extracts Claude credentials from the macOS Keychain.\n    85→func Credentials() error { return newOrch().ExtractCredentials() }\n    86→\n    87→// Analyze performs cross-artifact consistency checks (PRDs, use cases, test suites, roadmap).\n    88→func Analyze() error { return newOrch().Analyze() }\n    89→\n    90→// Tag creates a documentation release tag (v0.YYYYMMDD.N) and builds the container image.\n    91→func Tag() error { return newOrch().Tag() }\n    92→\n    93→// --- Scaffold targets ---\n    94→\n    95→// Pop removes orchestrator-managed files from the target repository:\n    96→// magefiles/orchestrator.go, docs/constitutions/, docs/prompts/, and\n    97→// configuration.yaml. Pass \".\" for the current directory.\n    98→func (Scaffold) Pop(target string) error { return newOrch().Uninstall(target) }\n    99→\n   100→// --- Cobbler targets ---\n   101→\n   102→// Measure assesses project state and proposes new tasks via Claude.\n   103→func (Cobbler) Measure() error { return newOrch().Measure() }\n   104→\n   105→// Stitch picks ready tasks and invokes Claude to execute them.\n   106→func (Cobbler) Stitch() error { return newOrch().Stitch() }\n   107→\n   108→// Reset removes the cobbler scratch directory.\n   109→func (Cobbler) Reset() error { return newOrch().CobblerReset() }\n   110→\n   111→// --- Generator targets ---\n   112→\n   113→// Start begins a new generation trail.\n   114→func (Generator) Start() error { return newOrch().GeneratorStart() }\n   115→\n   116→// Run executes measure + stitch cycles using the generation.cycles value in configuration.yaml.\n   117→// Use RunN to override the cycle count for a single invocation.\n   118→func (Generator) Run() error { return newOrch().GeneratorRun(0) }\n   119→\n   120→// RunN executes exactly n cycles of measure + stitch within the current generation.\n   121→// Pass n > 0 to override generation.cycles in configuration.yaml for this run only.\n   122→func (Generator) RunN(n int) error { return newOrch().GeneratorRun(n) }\n   123→\n   124→// Resume recovers from an interrupted run and continues.\n   125→func (Generator) Resume() error { return newOrch().GeneratorResume() }\n   126→\n   127→// Stop completes a generation trail and merges it into main.\n   128→func (Generator) Stop() error { return newOrch().GeneratorStop() }\n   129→\n   130→// List shows active branches and past generations.\n   131→func (Generator) List() error { return newOrch().GeneratorList() }\n   132→\n   133→// Switch commits current work and checks out another generation branch.\n   134→func (Generator) Switch() error { return newOrch().GeneratorSwitch() }\n   135→\n   136→// Reset destroys generation branches, worktrees, and Go source directories.\n   137→func (Generator) Reset() error { return newOrch().GeneratorReset() }\n   138→\n   139→// --- Stats targets ---\n   140→\n   141→// Loc prints Go lines of code and documentation word counts.\n   142→func (Stats) Loc() error { return newOrch().Stats() }\n   143→\n   144→// Tokens enumerates prompt-attached files and counts tokens via the Anthropic API.\n   145→func (Stats) Tokens() error { return newOrch().TokenStats() }\n   146→\n   147→// --- Prompt targets ---\n   148→\n   149→// Measure prints the assembled measure prompt to stdout.\n   150→func (Prompt) Measure() error { return newOrch().DumpMeasurePrompt() }\n   151→\n   152→// Stitch prints the assembled stitch prompt to stdout.\n   153→func (Prompt) Stitch() error { return newOrch().DumpStitchPrompt() }\n   154→\n   155→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1e27269-084c-48a0-81f5-e7539000574e","uuid":"ed0e326a-bfe0-4b5d-8014-098b5c5610e2","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/290/magefiles/orchestrator.go","content":"// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/magefile/mage/mg\"\n\t\"github.com/mesh-intelligence/cobbler-scaffold/pkg/orchestrator\"\n)\n\n// Cobbler groups the measure and stitch targets.\ntype Cobbler mg.Namespace\n\n// Generator groups the code-generation trail lifecycle targets.\ntype Generator mg.Namespace\n\n// Scaffold groups the scaffold install/uninstall targets.\ntype Scaffold mg.Namespace\n\n// Prompt groups prompt preview targets.\ntype Prompt mg.Namespace\n\n// Stats groups the stats targets (LOC, tokens).\ntype Stats mg.Namespace\n\n// Tests: run directly with go test:\n//   go test -tags=usecase -v -count=1 -timeout 1800s ./tests/rel01.0/...          # all\n//   go test -tags=usecase -v ./tests/rel01.0/uc001/                               # one UC\n//   go test -tags=usecase -bench=. -benchtime=1x -run=^$ ./tests/rel01.0/uc008/   # benchmarks\n\n// baseCfg holds the configuration loaded from configuration.yaml.\nvar baseCfg orchestrator.Config\n\nfunc init() {\n\tif _, err := os.Stat(orchestrator.DefaultConfigFile); errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\tif err := orchestrator.WriteDefaultConfig(orchestrator.DefaultConfigFile); err != nil {\n\t\t\tpanic(fmt.Sprintf(\"creating %s: %v\", orchestrator.DefaultConfigFile, err))\n\t\t}\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"created default %s\\n\", orchestrator.DefaultConfigFile)\n\t}\n\tvar err error\n\tbaseCfg, err = orchestrator.LoadConfig(orchestrator.DefaultConfigFile)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tpanic(fmt.Sprintf(\"loading %s: %v\", orchestrator.DefaultConfigFile, err))\n\t}\n}\n\n// newOrch creates an Orchestrator from the base config.\nfunc newOrch() *orchestrator.Orchestrator {\n\treturn orchestrator.New(baseCfg)\n}\n\n// logf prints a timestamped log line to stderr.\nfunc logf(format string, args ...any) {\n\tmsg := fmt.Sprintf(format, args...)\n\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"[%s] %s\\n\", time.Now().Format(time.RFC3339), msg)\n}\n\n// --- Top-level targets ---\n\n// Init initializes the project.\nfunc Init() error { return newOrch().Init() }\n\n// Reset performs a full reset: cobbler and generator.\nfunc Reset() error { return newOrch().FullReset() }\n\n// Build compiles the project binary.\nfunc Build() error { return newOrch().Build() }\n\n// Lint runs golangci-lint on the project.\nfunc Lint() error { return newOrch().Lint() }\n\n// Install runs go install for the main package.\nfunc Install() error { return newOrch().Install() }\n\n// Clean removes build artifacts.\nfunc Clean() error { return newOrch().Clean() }\n\n// Credentials extracts Claude credentials from the macOS Keychain.\nfunc Credentials() error { return newOrch().ExtractCredentials() }\n\n// Analyze performs cross-artifact consistency checks (PRDs, use cases, test suites, roadmap).\nfunc Analyze() error { return newOrch().Analyze() }\n\n// Tag creates a documentation release tag (v0.YYYYMMDD.N) and builds the container image.\nfunc Tag() error { return newOrch().Tag() }\n\n// --- Scaffold targets ---\n\n// Pop removes orchestrator-managed files from the target repository:\n// magefiles/orchestrator.go, docs/constitutions/, docs/prompts/, and\n// configuration.yaml. Pass \".\" for the current directory.\nfunc (Scaffold) Pop(target string) error { return newOrch().Uninstall(target) }\n\n// --- Cobbler targets ---\n\n// Measure assesses project state and proposes new tasks via Claude.\nfunc (Cobbler) Measure() error { return newOrch().Measure() }\n\n// Stitch picks ready tasks and invokes Claude to execute them.\nfunc (Cobbler) Stitch() error { return newOrch().Stitch() }\n\n// Reset removes the cobbler scratch directory.\nfunc (Cobbler) Reset() error { return newOrch().CobblerReset() }\n\n// --- Generator targets ---\n\n// Start begins a new generation trail.\nfunc (Generator) Start() error { return newOrch().GeneratorStart() }\n\n// Run executes measure + stitch cycles using the generation.cycles value in configuration.yaml.\n// Use RunN to override the cycle count for a single invocation.\nfunc (Generator) Run() error { return newOrch().GeneratorRun(0) }\n\n// RunN executes exactly n cycles of measure + stitch within the current generation.\n// Pass n > 0 to override generation.cycles in configuration.yaml for this run only.\nfunc (Generator) RunN(n int) error { return newOrch().GeneratorRun(n) }\n\n// Resume recovers from an interrupted run and continues.\nfunc (Generator) Resume() error { return newOrch().GeneratorResume() }\n\n// Stop completes a generation trail and merges it into main.\nfunc (Generator) Stop() error { return newOrch().GeneratorStop() }\n\n// List shows active branches and past generations.\nfunc (Generator) List() error { return newOrch().GeneratorList() }\n\n// Switch commits current work and checks out another generation branch.\nfunc (Generator) Switch() error { return newOrch().GeneratorSwitch() }\n\n// Reset destroys generation branches, worktrees, and Go source directories.\nfunc (Generator) Reset() error { return newOrch().GeneratorReset() }\n\n// --- Stats targets ---\n\n// Loc prints Go lines of code and documentation word counts.\nfunc (Stats) Loc() error { return newOrch().Stats() }\n\n// Tokens enumerates prompt-attached files and counts tokens via the Anthropic API.\nfunc (Stats) Tokens() error { return newOrch().TokenStats() }\n\n// --- Prompt targets ---\n\n// Measure prints the assembled measure prompt to stdout.\nfunc (Prompt) Measure() error { return newOrch().DumpMeasurePrompt() }\n\n// Stitch prints the assembled stitch prompt to stdout.\nfunc (Prompt) Stitch() error { return newOrch().DumpStitchPrompt() }\n\n","numLines":155,"startLine":1,"totalLines":155}}}
